WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:02.934
-With the midterms just
under five days away,

00:00:02.934 --> 00:00:05.334
Republicans have been hampered
by underperforming candidates

00:00:05.334 --> 00:00:06.734
in key races across the country

00:00:06.734 --> 00:00:08.501
and yet, still, several
of those candidates,

00:00:08.501 --> 00:00:10.634
including pro-Trump
election deniers

00:00:10.634 --> 00:00:12.234
who have outright declared

00:00:12.234 --> 00:00:14.634
that they will use their power
to steal future elections,

00:00:14.634 --> 00:00:16.767
are in very close races
and could easily win.

00:00:16.767 --> 00:00:18.767
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:18.767 --> 00:00:22.767
♪♪
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:22.767 --> 00:00:25.501
Historically, midterms just tend
to go very badly

00:00:25.501 --> 00:00:27.667
for the party in power
and the polls currently suggest

00:00:27.667 --> 00:00:29.701
that may, yet again,
be the case this year.

00:00:29.701 --> 00:00:32.434
The main thing holding
Republicans back, it seems,

00:00:32.434 --> 00:00:33.734
is that they've nominated some

00:00:33.734 --> 00:00:37.000
spectacularly [bleep]
candidates, like Mehmet Oz,

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:38.667
who's running for Senate
in Pennsylvania,

00:00:38.667 --> 00:00:41.667
but doesn't seem to know
exactly where Pennsylvania is.

00:00:41.667 --> 00:00:42.701
-Listen, this is important.

00:00:42.701 --> 00:00:44.634
We do not have
a Republican senator

00:00:44.634 --> 00:00:47.100
north of North Carolina
on the Atlantic Coast,

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:49.601
until you get the Maine,
if I don't hold this seat.

00:00:49.601 --> 00:00:51.434
-I'm no cartographer,
but I'm pretty sure

00:00:51.434 --> 00:00:53.534
Pennsylvania is not
on the Atlantic Coast.

00:00:53.534 --> 00:00:55.534
[ Laughter ]
You know how I know that?

00:00:55.534 --> 00:00:57.534
I have several staffers
who live in New Jersey

00:00:57.534 --> 00:00:59.267
and, whenever they come back
from summer hiatus,

00:00:59.267 --> 00:01:01.400
they always complain about all
the [bleep] Philly fans

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:02.501
down at the shore.

00:01:02.501 --> 00:01:03.601
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]

00:01:03.601 --> 00:01:06.367
I'm pretty sure Delaware
only exists

00:01:06.367 --> 00:01:09.000
to make it harder for Gritty
to get to the beach.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:10.334
[ Laughter ]

00:01:10.334 --> 00:01:11.534
You know how, also,
I know Pennsylvania isn't

00:01:11.534 --> 00:01:12.534
on the Atlantic Coast?

00:01:12.534 --> 00:01:13.901
There aren't any beaches
in Philadelphia.

00:01:13.901 --> 00:01:15.467
When they signed
the Declaration of Independence,

00:01:15.467 --> 00:01:17.434
they didn't celebrate
afterwards with a clambake.

00:01:17.434 --> 00:01:20.100
[ Laughter ]
Dr. Oz probably thinks
the Liberty Bell is there

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:22.300
to warn people when they spot
a shark in the water.

00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:23.934
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.934 --> 00:01:26.033
Then there's Georgia Senate
candidate Herschel Walker.

00:01:26.033 --> 00:01:28.133
The other day, President Obama
traveled to Georgia

00:01:28.133 --> 00:01:29.834
to campaign
for Walker's opponent,

00:01:29.834 --> 00:01:31.467
Democratic
Senator Raphael Warnock

00:01:31.467 --> 00:01:35.167
and this was Walker's response
to Obama's visit on Fox News.

00:01:35.167 --> 00:01:36.334
-I've created businesses.

00:01:36.334 --> 00:01:37.968
I sit on a publicly
traded board,

00:01:37.968 --> 00:01:40.534
so those are things I've done
outside of football.

00:01:40.534 --> 00:01:42.200
But my résumé
against his résumé,

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:44.067
I put it up any time of the day.

00:01:44.067 --> 00:01:45.834
-You do? That's like me saying,
[ Laughter ]

00:01:45.834 --> 00:01:47.934
"Einstein?
I'm way smarter than him.

00:01:47.934 --> 00:01:49.334
[ Laughter ]
That dope could never do

00:01:49.334 --> 00:01:51.100
a 'Day Drinking'
with Post Malone."

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:53.434
[ Laughter ]

00:01:53.434 --> 00:01:55.667
Look, you don't have
Obama's résumé.

00:01:55.667 --> 00:01:57.801
You know how I know?
Obama never had to flash

00:01:57.801 --> 00:01:59.434
a fake sheriff's badge
in a debate

00:01:59.434 --> 00:02:01.467
like he was cosplaying
as Deputy Dog.

00:02:01.467 --> 00:02:02.834
[ Laughter ]
Dude

00:02:02.834 --> 00:02:04.534
was president
of the Harvard Law Review,

00:02:04.534 --> 00:02:06.834
a senator, president,
he's won a Grammy and Emmy,

00:02:06.834 --> 00:02:08.400
he was Time's
Person of the Year,

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:10.033
he went kitesurfing
with Richard Branson,

00:02:10.033 --> 00:02:12.234
and now, he's got a Netflix deal
where he produces movies

00:02:12.234 --> 00:02:15.133
and he still manages
to maintain that laidback style

00:02:15.133 --> 00:02:16.767
he's got going on
post-presidency.

00:02:16.767 --> 00:02:18.300
He could climb
to the top of Everest

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:20.234
and, somehow,
he'd still have shades on

00:02:20.234 --> 00:02:22.000
and at least two shirt
buttons undone.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:23.167
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.167 --> 00:02:24.767
[ As Obama ]
Uh...decided to climb Everest

00:02:24.767 --> 00:02:26.267
because it's, uh, here.

00:02:26.267 --> 00:02:29.067
[ Laughter ]
Also, it's, uh, the only place

00:02:29.067 --> 00:02:31.200
I can smoke without, uh,
Michelle finding out.

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:34.434
[ Laughter ]

00:02:34.434 --> 00:02:35.734
So, we're in a weird place.

00:02:35.734 --> 00:02:38.000
On the one hand, these midterms
are, in some ways,

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:40.400
very normal, very predictable,
and yet, on the other hand,

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:43.200
these midterms are,
in many ways, very abnormal

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:45.801
and, potentially, catastrophic
for our democracy because,

00:02:45.801 --> 00:02:48.033
as we've explained, it's very
typical for the party in power

00:02:48.033 --> 00:02:49.667
to lose seats
in a midterm election.

00:02:49.667 --> 00:02:50.734
That's just how it always goes.

00:02:50.734 --> 00:02:52.267
Political scientists call it

00:02:52.267 --> 00:02:54.067
thermostatic public opinion.

00:02:54.067 --> 00:02:57.033
People just like to go back
and forth to keep things even.

00:02:57.033 --> 00:02:59.601
In this analogy,
the government is a thermostat

00:02:59.601 --> 00:03:00.834
and the electorate is your dad,

00:03:00.834 --> 00:03:02.234
when you go home
for the holidays.

00:03:02.234 --> 00:03:04.067
If you put it up to 70°,
he's immediately going to come

00:03:04.067 --> 00:03:05.334
and put it back to 68°.

00:03:05.334 --> 00:03:06.767
If you put it down to 66°,

00:03:06.767 --> 00:03:09.167
he's going to immediately come
back and set it to 68°.

00:03:09.167 --> 00:03:10.801
And, if you bring home
a college girlfriend

00:03:10.801 --> 00:03:13.067
for the holidays, who's a vegan
and doesn't shave her legs,

00:03:13.067 --> 00:03:15.200
he'll turn it up to 85°,
in an effort to sweat her out

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:16.200
and make her leave early.

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:17.267
[ Laughter ]
And it worked, Dad!

00:03:17.267 --> 00:03:18.868
Congratulations!

00:03:18.868 --> 00:03:20.501
You chased Sparrow
out of my life

00:03:20.501 --> 00:03:22.934
and not a day goes by
that I don't hate you for it!

00:03:22.934 --> 00:03:24.968
[ Laughter ]
And I'm sorry, everybody,

00:03:24.968 --> 00:03:26.834
I'm just between therapists
right now.

00:03:26.834 --> 00:03:28.167
[ Laughter ]

00:03:28.167 --> 00:03:30.267
I had a great therapist,
but she kept her thermostat

00:03:30.267 --> 00:03:32.133
at 74°, like a psycho.

00:03:32.133 --> 00:03:33.400
[ Laughter ]

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:34.501
Anyway, the point is,

00:03:34.501 --> 00:03:35.801
on the one hand,
it would be totally normal

00:03:35.801 --> 00:03:37.334
and, in many ways,
completely unremarkable

00:03:37.334 --> 00:03:39.501
for Democrats to lose seats
in next week's midterms.

00:03:39.501 --> 00:03:41.901
However, it's now
incredibly abnormal

00:03:41.901 --> 00:03:43.133
and, potentially, very dangerous

00:03:43.133 --> 00:03:45.200
because one of our two
major political parties

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:46.767
is fundamentally opposed
to democracy.

00:03:46.767 --> 00:03:48.501
They simply don't accept

00:03:48.501 --> 00:03:50.367
the outcomes
of elections they don't win,

00:03:50.367 --> 00:03:51.968
they wage coups when they lose,

00:03:51.968 --> 00:03:54.133
and they openly announced
their intention

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:56.100
to rig future elections,
if they take power.

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:58.868
For example, the GOP candidate
for governor in Wisconsin

00:03:58.868 --> 00:04:02.000
is a guy named Tim Michels,
a pro-Trump election denier

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:03.367
who believes,
without any evidence,

00:04:03.367 --> 00:04:05.300
that the 2020 election
was stolen

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:07.934
and he just said it out loud
in the open the other day.

00:04:07.934 --> 00:04:09.267
He just declared that,
if he wins,

00:04:09.267 --> 00:04:11.567
he will use his power
to make sure Democrats

00:04:11.567 --> 00:04:13.968
never win another election,
ever again.

00:04:13.968 --> 00:04:16.367
Here's what he said
at a recent campaign stop.

00:04:21.334 --> 00:04:22.834
[ Applause and whistling ]
-Yeah!

00:04:22.834 --> 00:04:24.467
Yay!
-Whoo!

00:04:24.467 --> 00:04:26.234
-My favorite part of that clip
is someone off-camera

00:04:26.234 --> 00:04:28.200
at the very end going, "Yay!

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:29.868
[ Laughter ]
Yay!" Like they're

00:04:29.868 --> 00:04:31.734
at their five-year-old's
first T-ball game.

00:04:31.734 --> 00:04:33.601
Yay, Timmy!

00:04:33.601 --> 00:04:36.300
You did it, fascism, yay!

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:37.534
[ Laughter ]

00:04:37.534 --> 00:04:40.267
Does this guy know he's
in public, on-camera,

00:04:40.267 --> 00:04:42.067
with like reporters
and people around?

00:04:42.067 --> 00:04:43.400
Because he just admitted
to something

00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:44.267
incredibly nefarious.

00:04:44.267 --> 00:04:45.567
It's like if a Bond villain

00:04:45.567 --> 00:04:48.000
livestreamed their plan
to kill Bond on Instagram.

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:49.334
[ Changes accent ]
Hello, what's up, Instagram?

00:04:49.334 --> 00:04:50.501
It's your boy Blofeld.

00:04:50.501 --> 00:04:52.000
[ Laughter ]

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:53.701
Just wanted to go live
to let you know

00:04:53.701 --> 00:04:55.467
about my plan to kill James!

00:04:55.467 --> 00:04:56.667
[ Laughter ]

00:04:56.667 --> 00:04:58.868
I'm going to lure him
into my underground lair

00:04:58.868 --> 00:05:00.501
by capturing
his romantic interest

00:05:00.501 --> 00:05:03.167
and then slowly lower him
into a tank full of sharks.

00:05:03.167 --> 00:05:05.834
If you like this plan, feel free
to let me know in the comments.

00:05:05.834 --> 00:05:08.300
Oh, I see a lot of hearts
and emojis!

00:05:08.300 --> 00:05:10.133
[ Laughter ]
A lot of fire emojis.

00:05:10.133 --> 00:05:12.033
Oh, too bad, James.
They like it.

00:05:12.033 --> 00:05:14.033
[ Laughter ]

00:05:14.033 --> 00:05:15.400
So, they're not even
hiding it anymore.

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:17.067
They're just
out in the open about it.

00:05:17.067 --> 00:05:19.200
If Republicans take power,
they will make sure

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:21.200
that only Republicans win
future elections.

00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:22.901
It's that simple
and there are a few states

00:05:22.901 --> 00:05:25.300
where that threat
is especially acute.

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:27.200
In Arizona, for example,
Republicans have nominated

00:05:27.200 --> 00:05:30.234
a former local television
personality named Kari Lake,

00:05:30.234 --> 00:05:32.934
a hardline,
pro-Trump election denier.

00:05:32.934 --> 00:05:35.634
Has said she will also
use her power in Arizona,

00:05:35.634 --> 00:05:37.133
if she wins,
to undermine elections.

00:05:37.133 --> 00:05:39.734
She's even gone so far
to insist, without evidence,

00:05:39.734 --> 00:05:41.667
that there's no way
Joe Biden got

00:05:41.667 --> 00:05:43.400
the number of votes
he definitely got.

00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:46.567
-They actually made a joke
of our elections

00:05:46.567 --> 00:05:48.000
and I'm really...

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:49.367
pissed off about it.

00:05:49.367 --> 00:05:50.634
[ Applause ]

00:05:50.634 --> 00:05:52.667
And I'm going to do
something about.

00:05:52.667 --> 00:05:56.734
So, it is literally
unconstitutional, what they did.

00:05:56.734 --> 00:06:01.634
The truth is that Joe Biden did
not win with 81 million votes.

00:06:01.634 --> 00:06:04.167
[ Crowd murmuring ]

00:06:04.167 --> 00:06:07.634
And, if you believe he did,

00:06:07.634 --> 00:06:10.634
then you are
the conspiracy theorist.

00:06:10.634 --> 00:06:12.000
-Jesus!
That lady is creepier

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:14.267
than one of those
Boston Dynamics robots.

00:06:14.267 --> 00:06:15.634
[ Laughter ]

00:06:15.634 --> 00:06:18.167
Got the vibe of a Realtor
who insists on putting her face

00:06:18.167 --> 00:06:19.901
on all of her for sale signs.

00:06:19.901 --> 00:06:21.300
[ Laughter ]

00:06:21.300 --> 00:06:23.434
But the thing about Lake is
she's much slicker

00:06:23.434 --> 00:06:24.767
than most of the other weirdos

00:06:24.767 --> 00:06:26.167
the Republicans
have nominated this year,

00:06:26.167 --> 00:06:28.467
even if her beliefs
are just as loony.

00:06:28.467 --> 00:06:30.367
She's a longtime
local television personality

00:06:30.367 --> 00:06:32.501
in the Phoenix area,
so a lot of people know her.

00:06:32.501 --> 00:06:33.767
She even knows how
to light herself

00:06:33.767 --> 00:06:35.133
when she does interviews
from her home,

00:06:35.133 --> 00:06:37.300
as you can tell,
every time she's on TV,

00:06:37.300 --> 00:06:39.367
and she apparently
has her ring light

00:06:39.367 --> 00:06:40.934
turned all the way up to 11.

00:06:40.934 --> 00:06:42.133
[ Laughter ]

00:06:42.133 --> 00:06:43.968
My real takeaway here
isn't how good she looks.

00:06:43.968 --> 00:06:47.100
It's how [bleep] up every other
politician looks from home.

00:06:47.100 --> 00:06:48.667
I mean, is there anything
more depressing

00:06:48.667 --> 00:06:50.267
than when members of Congress
try to grill

00:06:50.267 --> 00:06:51.767
major tech titans
during a hearing

00:06:51.767 --> 00:06:53.901
and they show up with only
the top half of their head

00:06:53.901 --> 00:06:55.501
in the frame,
looking into the wrong camera?

00:06:55.501 --> 00:06:57.667
Our politicians
should look better

00:06:57.667 --> 00:06:59.267
than our cue card guy,
Wally, did

00:06:59.267 --> 00:07:01.801
during a mandatory respect
in the workplace Zoom meeting.

00:07:01.801 --> 00:07:03.634
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:03.634 --> 00:07:07.267
A real non-Photoshopped
picture...

00:07:07.267 --> 00:07:09.100
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:09.100 --> 00:07:10.634
...that I took on my phone,

00:07:10.634 --> 00:07:14.267
and so did every other [bleep]
person who works here.

00:07:14.267 --> 00:07:15.834
[ Laughter ]

00:07:15.834 --> 00:07:17.400
You should've
seen the text chain.

00:07:17.400 --> 00:07:18.200
"Have you seen Wa--"

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:19.767
I've seen Wally.

00:07:19.767 --> 00:07:22.501
[ Laughter ]

00:07:24.667 --> 00:07:26.501
By contrast,
Lake looks so polished,

00:07:26.501 --> 00:07:27.667
she might be CGI.

00:07:27.667 --> 00:07:29.601
If she weren't running
for governor in Arizona,

00:07:29.601 --> 00:07:30.701
I'd think she was the character

00:07:30.701 --> 00:07:32.100
from one of those '90s
video games

00:07:32.100 --> 00:07:33.133
who gives you your mission.

00:07:33.133 --> 00:07:34.334
[ As Lake ]
This is Admiral Lake.

00:07:34.334 --> 00:07:36.934
If you collect...
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:42.300 --> 00:07:43.901
That's how you know
someone's a little too slick.

00:07:43.901 --> 00:07:45.901
Like I've been on TV
for 20 years

00:07:45.901 --> 00:07:47.267
and, when I started doing
at-home shows

00:07:47.267 --> 00:07:48.534
for the first time,
I was so pale,

00:07:48.534 --> 00:07:50.334
I looked like
Jared Kushner's ghost.

00:07:50.334 --> 00:07:51.801
[ Laughter ]
I didn't even know

00:07:51.801 --> 00:07:53.167
what a ring light was.

00:07:53.167 --> 00:07:54.234
When they finally sent me one,

00:07:54.234 --> 00:07:55.734
I thought it was
a light-up toilet seat.

00:07:55.734 --> 00:07:57.934
[ Laughter ]
I was like, "Oh, this is cool.

00:07:57.934 --> 00:07:58.734
Good news, kids!

00:07:58.734 --> 00:08:00.167
You can [bleep] in the dark now.

00:08:00.167 --> 00:08:01.767
[ Laughter ]

00:08:01.767 --> 00:08:04.200
Don't wake up Daddy anymore.

00:08:04.200 --> 00:08:05.200
Oh, you're going to love it.

00:08:05.200 --> 00:08:06.801
It's like peeing
into Yankee Stadium

00:08:06.801 --> 00:08:08.033
from a hot air balloon."

00:08:08.033 --> 00:08:10.767
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:14.767 --> 00:08:16.601
But Lake is a slick
TV personality,

00:08:16.601 --> 00:08:19.033
which is why she's got so much
sway with Trump's MAGA base,

00:08:19.033 --> 00:08:20.534
and President Obama
made note of that

00:08:20.534 --> 00:08:22.033
during a trip to Arizona
on Wednesday

00:08:22.033 --> 00:08:23.934
to campaign for the Democratic
nominee for governor,

00:08:23.934 --> 00:08:26.033
Katie Hobbs.
Obama pointed out something

00:08:26.033 --> 00:08:27.334
we should know
from recent experience --

00:08:27.334 --> 00:08:29.100
just because you know someone
from TV

00:08:29.100 --> 00:08:31.567
doesn't mean they'd be
a good elected official.

00:08:31.567 --> 00:08:34.100
-Here in Arizona.

00:08:34.100 --> 00:08:37.334
there's no question that
Katie Hobbs' opponent,

00:08:37.334 --> 00:08:38.601
she's good in front
of the camera

00:08:38.601 --> 00:08:41.067
because she's been doing it
for a long time.

00:08:41.067 --> 00:08:45.467
Listen, if we hadn't
just elected somebody

00:08:45.467 --> 00:08:47.834
whose main qualification
was being on TV...

00:08:47.834 --> 00:08:49.667
[ Laughter ]

00:08:49.667 --> 00:08:52.567
...you could see maybe
giving it a shot.

00:08:52.567 --> 00:08:54.701
What's the worst
that could happen?

00:08:54.701 --> 00:08:55.968
Well, now, we know!

00:08:55.968 --> 00:08:58.200
[ Cheering and applause ]
It doesn't just work out

00:08:58.200 --> 00:09:00.501
just because somebody's been
on TV.

00:09:00.501 --> 00:09:01.634
-[ Laughs ]
Obama --

00:09:01.634 --> 00:09:02.901
At what point
do we learn our lesson?

00:09:02.901 --> 00:09:05.133
We can just keep cycling
through TV idiots,

00:09:05.133 --> 00:09:06.300
until we end up
with a government

00:09:06.300 --> 00:09:08.534
that's just filled with the cast
of "FBOY Island."

00:09:08.534 --> 00:09:09.968
[ Laughter ]

00:09:09.968 --> 00:09:11.734
Maybe, from now on,
instead of holding elections,

00:09:11.734 --> 00:09:13.133
we should just make
our candidates run

00:09:13.133 --> 00:09:14.834
through a reality TV
obstacle course

00:09:14.834 --> 00:09:16.367
and whoever makes it to the end
becomes president.

00:09:16.367 --> 00:09:18.868
I mean, I'd love to see Trump
try to make it

00:09:18.868 --> 00:09:21.133
through the course
from "American Ninja Warrior."

00:09:21.133 --> 00:09:23.734
[ Laughter ]
He'd try to jump
over those floating tiles

00:09:23.734 --> 00:09:25.501
and immediately end up
in the water.

00:09:25.501 --> 00:09:27.501
[ Electronic music ]

00:09:27.501 --> 00:09:28.934
[ Warbling, splash ]

00:09:28.934 --> 00:09:31.133
[ Reverberating powerdown ]

00:09:31.133 --> 00:09:33.367
[ Laughter ]
That's from that Kari Lake
video game.

00:09:33.367 --> 00:09:36.667
[ Laughter ]

00:09:36.667 --> 00:09:38.601
Ten guys worked all week.

00:09:38.601 --> 00:09:42.234
[ Laughter ]

00:09:42.234 --> 00:09:44.167
Obama even got specific

00:09:44.167 --> 00:09:45.901
about Lake's deranged
election claims,

00:09:45.901 --> 00:09:47.868
pointing out that even
some fellow Republicans

00:09:47.868 --> 00:09:50.067
have debunked them,
and he also, in that same clip,

00:09:50.067 --> 00:09:51.968
knocked her again
for her TV experience.

00:09:51.968 --> 00:09:55.234
-The other day, your own
current attorney general,

00:09:55.234 --> 00:09:57.334
who's a Republican...
-Yeah!

00:09:57.334 --> 00:09:59.367
-...called the election
fraud claims made

00:09:59.367 --> 00:10:02.601
by Katie Hobbs' opponent
horse crap.

00:10:02.601 --> 00:10:03.901
[ Cheering and applause ]
I'm paraphrasing.

00:10:03.901 --> 00:10:06.834
He didn't say it exactly
that way.

00:10:06.834 --> 00:10:08.067
He said her whole act

00:10:08.067 --> 00:10:12.701
about how the election was
stolen is a giant grift.

00:10:12.701 --> 00:10:14.534
Why would you vote for somebody
who you know

00:10:14.534 --> 00:10:16.434
is not telling the truth
about something?

00:10:16.434 --> 00:10:18.567
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:10:18.567 --> 00:10:21.701
I mean,
on something that important.

00:10:23.400 --> 00:10:26.267
I don't care how nicely
they say it.

00:10:26.267 --> 00:10:29.334
I don't care
how poised they are

00:10:29.334 --> 00:10:31.434
or how well-lit they are.

00:10:31.434 --> 00:10:33.400
[ Laughter ]

00:10:33.400 --> 00:10:36.000
-I love that Obama made fun
of how well-lit she is.

00:10:36.000 --> 00:10:38.033
It's such a specific dig,

00:10:38.033 --> 00:10:41.634
but it also proves that he is
in the TV business now, too.

00:10:41.634 --> 00:10:43.467
[ As Obama ]
And how good is her sound?

00:10:43.467 --> 00:10:45.467
I mean, what's she using,
a Sennheiser G4

00:10:45.467 --> 00:10:48.234
with an omnidirectional
polar pattern?

00:10:48.234 --> 00:10:49.734
She's not popping her bass.

00:10:49.734 --> 00:10:52.200
[ Laughter ]

00:10:52.200 --> 00:10:53.801
But he's right
about the core point --

00:10:53.801 --> 00:10:55.200
this is all deranged

00:10:55.200 --> 00:10:57.834
and it's all very much a part
of a coordinated strategy.

00:10:57.834 --> 00:10:59.968
Trump handpicked a lot
of these people specifically

00:10:59.968 --> 00:11:01.067
because he wanted to put them

00:11:01.067 --> 00:11:02.267
in positions of power
in Congress

00:11:02.267 --> 00:11:03.968
and in key swing states
around the country,

00:11:03.968 --> 00:11:05.234
so they could help him succeed

00:11:05.234 --> 00:11:06.968
with the attempted coup
he failed that in 2020.

00:11:06.968 --> 00:11:08.667
Trump wants people like Lake
and Michels

00:11:08.667 --> 00:11:11.334
in positions of power
in states he lost last time,

00:11:11.334 --> 00:11:13.000
so they can help him cheat
next time,

00:11:13.000 --> 00:11:15.067
because Trump has never
stopped obsessing

00:11:15.067 --> 00:11:16.667
over his 2020 election loss.

00:11:16.667 --> 00:11:18.400
He's been stewing about it
ever since.

00:11:18.400 --> 00:11:21.133
That's why he always looks like
he just stepped in some...

00:11:21.133 --> 00:11:22.334
-Horse crap.

00:11:22.334 --> 00:11:23.801
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:11:23.801 --> 00:11:27.434
♪♪

00:11:27.434 --> 00:11:29.234
The midterm elections
are coming up, so,

00:11:29.234 --> 00:11:31.834
to make sure that you're good
to vote in this election,

00:11:31.834 --> 00:11:34.901
visit our good friends
at headcount.org

00:11:34.901 --> 00:11:38.968
to check your voter registration
status or to register to vote.

